cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ForestPro: a browser-based platform for forest inventory, mensuration, biomass, carbon and agroforestry"
abstract: >-
  ForestPro is a self-contained web application that carries a forest or agroforestry inventory from the
  field sheet to the report in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It covers
  tree mensuration (basal area, log and stem volume by Huber, Smalian and Newton, form factor, volume
  equations, segmented taper and height–diameter models fitted by nonlinear least squares), inventory and
  sampling (simple random, stratified, systematic and cluster designs, nested and point sampling, sample size,
  stand tables, Weibull diameter distributions, importance value, stand density and competition indices),
  biomass and carbon (an editable catalogue of allometric equations, wood density from the Global Wood
  Density Database, root-to-shoot ratios, deadwood, litter and soil carbon, Monte Carlo propagation of error
  and stock change), growth and yield (increments, growth models, site index, a whole-stand projection),
  diversity (Shannon, Simpson, Fisher, Chao, Hill numbers, rarefaction, dissimilarity, ordination,
  vertical structure, Clark–Evans and Ripley's K), agroforestry (shade from the inventory or a hemispherical
  photograph, shade–yield response, planting layouts, carbon budget), maps (own map with optional
  OpenStreetMap background, polygon areas, sampling grids, GPX/KML/GeoJSON export, IDW and kriging) and
  forestry tools (log rules, lumber, sawmill yield, unit conversions, plantation economics), and writes a
  self-contained report. Bilingual interface (Spanish and English). Every block was checked against
  independent references in R with stated tolerances (8,327 comparisons, no disagreements), and 84 unit
  tests run in the browser.
type: software
